Non-Browser Process Access to Browser Credential Files

This threat hunting scenario is designed to detect non-browser processes attempting to access sensitive browser credential files such as Login Data, Cookies, and browser state files. This behavior can indicate credential theft or information-stealing malware attempting to access saved passwords, session cookies, autofill data, and other sensitive browser information. The scenario focuses on identifying processes that are not recognized as legitimate web browsers while accessing these credential stores, which may indicate potential infostealer activity and should be investigated further.

MITRE ATT&CK Techniques:

T1555.003 – Credentials from Web Browsers
Attackers may access browser credential stores to steal saved passwords, cookies, session tokens, and other authentication data.
T1539 – Steal Web Session Cookie
Attackers may access browser cookie stores to obtain valid session cookies and potentially bypass authentication.
T1005 – Data from Local System
Malicious processes may collect sensitive credential and browser-related data stored locally on the endpoint.

Coretex:

dataset = xdr_data
| alter
    username = os_actor_primary_username,
    src_process = actor_process_image_name,
    src_cmdline = actor_process_command_line,
    src_path = actor_process_image_path,
    target_file = action_file_path
| filter event_type = ENUM.FILE and event_sub_type = ENUM.FILE_OPEN
| filter action_file_path ~= "(?i)(Login Data|Cookies|Web Data|Local State|logins\.json|cookies\.sqlite|key[34]\.db)"
| filter action_file_path ~= "(?i)(Chrome|Edge|BraveSoftware|Chromium|Firefox|Opera)"
| filter src_process not in ("chrome.exe", "msedge.exe", "brave.exe", "chromium.exe", "firefox.exe", "opera.exe", "chrome", "Google Chrome", "msedge", "brave", "chromium", "firefox", "opera", "AcroRd32.exe", "Acrobat.exe", "svchost.exe", "AdobeCollabSync.exe", "FirefoxPortable.exe", "RdrServicesUpdater2_x86.exe", "Brave Browser", "Microsoft Edge")
| filter username != "NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM" and username != "AUTORITE NT\Système"
| filter target_file not contains "Palo Alto Networks"
| fields _time, agent_hostname, username, src_process, src_path, src_cmdline, target_file
